<block
  xmlns="http://blockml.org/schema/block"
  xmlns:xsi="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema-instance"
  xsi:schemaLocation="http://blockml.org/schema/block https://blockml.org/schemas/core/block.xsd"
  xmlns:core="org.blockml.bml.core"
  xmlns:type="org.blockml.bml.type">
  <name>Boolean</name>
  <type>type:Boolean</type>
  <baseType>type:PrimitiveType</baseType>
  <is>A true-or-false value</is>

  <documentation>BOM Core primitive ValueType for true/false values. Unqualified name Boolean
    resolves to org.blockml.bml.type.Boolean. Boolean is neither textual nor numeric — its own
    primitive branch. Values are stored in Properties — not on the Boolean type itself.

    Authoring accepts case variants of the literals: true / True / TRUE and false / False / FALSE.
    Preferred form is lowercase true and false. The BOM always stores the canonical boolean
    (lowercase true or false) — never the authored casing.</documentation>
</block>